      "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =3,$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ opposite to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{15}{BC} \\\\ BC & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\ BC & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =37.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
